S - Save Point   X - Inaccessible   C - Chest you can&#x27;t get yet
1 - Holy Water   2 - Breeze Armlet  3 - Celestial Tea (hidden behind tree)</pre>
      </AsciiMap>

      <p><Tag type="enemy">Feepos</Tag> can randomly drop a <Tag type="weapon">Vital Sword</Tag>, which would be really nice for <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>. You cannot procure any of the treasures yet. Go west to the <Tag type="place">Highway</Tag> and down the ramp to revise your destination. Walk south to the <Tag type="place">Woodland Path East</Tag>, west around the river, and north to the other side of the river. Choosing to &quot;Go to <Tag type="place">Alma Mine</Tag>&quot; will unlock [The Queen Ascendant] ending.</p>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: The Messenger&#x27;s News">
        <p>If you choose to stay with <Tag type="char">Heiss</Tag> first, you will need to return to &quot;The Beginning&quot; node and choose to Join the Rosch Brigade. If you need to do that, then skip back to Chapter 03 (Alistel - Alternate Prologue). Otherwise, return to &quot;The Messenger&#x27;s News&quot; node, and choose to &quot;Wait for Informant&quot;.</p>
      </Callout>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: No-Show">
        <p>Go south one screen and west to the <Tag type="place">Woodland Path</Tag>. Along the way, you will hear something.</p>
      </Callout>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Echoing Hills">
        <p>Heal everyone up and continue north to find out what&#x27;s making all the ruckus.</p>
      </Callout>

      <BossCard
        name="Desert Pirate Hertz, Red Sand Bram"
        weakness="None"
      >
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Ideally, you want everyone to take their turns in one round. Use <Tag type="skill">Change</Tag>, as needed. Have <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag> <Tag type="skill">Grapple</Tag> Hertz, <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag> cast <Tag type="skill">Thunder</Tag>, and <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag> use <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> to reduce their damage output. In subsequent rounds, Stocke should finish the combo with <Tag type="skill">Power Wave</Tag>. Only heal if your HP drops below 100.</p>
      </BossCard>

      <p>For defeating them, you will have saved the merchant <Tag type="char">Tarquin</Tag>. In return, he will teach you the <Tag type="skill">Bomber Skill</Tag>. This will also allow you to proceed back at <Tag type="place">Alma Mine</Tag> in Alternate History. If you want to do so, then skip ahead to Chapter 12 (Alma Mine - Alternate Prologue).</p>

      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Struggle with Bandits">
        <p>Before proceeding with your mission, let&#x27;s put that new bomber skill to use. Remember all those barrels we&#x27;ve seen along the way? Apparently, people just leave them full of explosives in this world. Go back east to the next screen and north until you see some barrels on the right. Push one of them around to the rocks on the left. Press L to prime the explosive, back away, and press L again to detonate them and blow away the rocks. Behind them is a chest which contains a <Tag type="item">Holy Water</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>

      <p>Return north to where you met the spy and enter the cave. Sadly, the soldier trapped there has died. Fortunately, you can use the barrel to gain access to the chest next to him which contains a <Tag type="acc">Breeze Armlet</Tag> (SPD+1, equip on <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>). Examine the corpse to receive the [Accident in the Cave] sidequest. If only we could have saved him before this occurred. It would be rather inconvenient to do so right now, and he&#x27;s not going anywhere for awhile.</p>

      <p>There is yet another barrel at the entrance by the right side of <Tag type="place">Highway East</Tag>. Push it down and blow away the rocks to reach the <Tag type="place">Southern Path</Tag>. Behind the tree on the right is a chest which contains <Tag type="item">Celestial Tea</Tag>. You may want to return to <Tag type="place">Alistel</Tag> to rest up at the <Tag type="place">Inn</Tag>. Otherwise, return to the <Tag type="place">Woodland Path</Tag>, go west and south to reach <Tag type="place">Judgement Cliff</Tag>.</p>

      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Custom Sword</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Beast Skins</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Charm</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Breeze Armlet</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Light Lance</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Brigandine</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Bronze Sword</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Bronze Mail</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 09 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch09"
    number={9}
    title="Judgement Cliff (Standard Chapter 1)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
