      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Breakthrough">
        <p>There is no treasure to be found here for now, so it&#x27;s very straight-forward. In the <Tag type="place">Sand Fortress South</Tag> area, hug the west cliffs to avoid stepping on any traps on the main road. Before entering the fortress, you will also find a merchant. I would recommend buying <Tag type="acc">6 Fang Charms</Tag>, giving 3 of each to <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag> and <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>. A <Tag type="weapon">Rune Spear</Tag> will greatly boost <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag>&#x27;s magic stat. All of these will last you for a very long time. However, I&#x27;d save the remaining money for buying armor later. You can also buy <Tag type="item">2 Anti-Sleeps</Tag> for the [Night Watch] sidequest, which we&#x27;ll be completing soon enough. If you can afford it, I would also purchase a <Tag type="weapon">Rune Edge</Tag> for <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>. Maybe try buying it after looting some of the soldiers. Hand down his old <Tag type="weapon">Custom Sword</Tag> to <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag>.</p>
      </Callout>

      <p>The path through the <Tag type="place">Sand Fortress</Tag> can be very short. If you just walk right up the middle staircases, you can make it up to the <Tag type="place">3rd Floor</Tag> without a fight. Then, walk around to the right and up the stairs to the exit. However, I&#x27;d strongly recommend fighting every soldier that you can, just for the gold and experience. Plus, you still might pick up a <Tag type="weapon">Vital Blade</Tag> from the <Tag type="enemy">Feepos</Tag> around here too. When you&#x27;re ready, go through the door atop the third floor for your last trial.</p>

      <BossCard
        name="Granorg Defender, Granorg Archer x2, Light Granorgite x2"
        weakness="None"
      >
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> <Tag type="char">Marco</Tag> should cast <Tag type="skill">Magic Boost</Tag> on <Tag type="char">Raynie</Tag> and <Tag type="char">Stocke</Tag>, while they use <Tag type="skill">Push Assault</Tag> and <Tag type="skill">Thunder</Tag> to take out a <Tag type="enemy">Light Granorgite</Tag> and <Tag type="enemy">Granorg Archer</Tag>. Once they&#x27;re all out of the way, I would use the <Tag type="skill">Change</Tag> command to string together six consecutive turns of alternating between physical attacks and spells to finish off the <Tag type="enemy">Granorg Defender</Tag>.</p>
      </BossCard>

      <p>For defeating them, you will gain access to the <Tag type="place">Sand Fortress North</Tag> area. The exit can be found to the northeast. Before continuing on to the <Tag type="place">Gran Plain</Tag>, you should rest up back at <Tag type="place">Alistel</Tag>.</p>

      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game:<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Edge</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Beast Skins</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Rune Spear</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Brigandine</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Horn Charm x3</Tag><br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> <Tag type="weapon">Custom Sword</Tag>, <Tag type="armor">Bronze Mail</Tag>, <Tag type="acc">Fang Charm x3</Tag></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
